mes>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Bonjer</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Jeekel</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Meta-analysis of techniques for closure of midline abdominal incisions</article-title><source>Br J Surg</source><year>2002</year><volume>89</volume><fpage>1350</fpage><lpage>1356</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12390373</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1365-2168.2002.02258.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Krukowski</surname><given-names>ZH</given-names></name><name><surname>Cusick</surname><given-names>EL</given-names></name><name><surname>Engeset</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Matheson</surname><given-names>NA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Polydioxanone or polypropylene for closure of midline abdominal incisions: a prospective comparative clinical trial</article-title><source>Br J Surg</source><year>1987</year><volume>74</volume><fpage>828</fpage><lpage>830</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3117165</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/bjs.1800740927</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cameron</surname><given-names>AE</given-names></name><name><surname>Parker</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Field</surname><given-names>ES</given-names></name><name><surname>Gray</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name><name><surname>Wyatt</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A randomised comparison of polydioxanone (PDS) and polypropylene (Prolene) for abdominal wound closure</article-title><source>Ann R Coll Surg Engl</source><year>1987</year><volume>69</volume><fpage>113</fpage><lpage>115</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3111339</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Weiland</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name><name><surname>Bay</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name><name><surname>Del</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Choosing the best abdominal closure by meta-analysis</article-title><source>Am J Surg</source><year>1998</year><volume>176</volume><fpage>666</fpage><lpage>670</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9926810</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0002-9610(98)00277-3</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hodgson</surname><given-names>NC</given-names></name><name><surname>Malthaner</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Ostbye</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The search for an ideal method of abdominal fascial closure: a meta-analysis</article-title><source>Ann Surg</source><year>2000</year><volume>231</volume><fpage>436</fpage><lpage>442</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10714638</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00000658-200003000-00018</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rucinski</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Margolis</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Panagopoulos</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Wise</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Closure of the abdominal midline fascia: meta-analysis delineates the optimal technique</article-title><source>Am Surg</source><year>2001</year><volume>67</volume><fpage>421</fpage><lpage>426</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11379640</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Knaebel</surname><g